Section 1.5.2 here tells you what to do to get started with all of the tidyverse including ggplot2.

http://r4ds.had.co.nz/introduction.html#getting-help-and-learning-more

Download R and install packages according to those instructions. Then once you've done that read through to Chapter 3: http://r4ds.had.co.nz/data-visualisation.html

The R4DataScience chapters should get you started. There is also a new version of the ggplot2 book.
https://www.amazon.com/ggplot2-Elegant-Graphics-Data-Analysis/dp/331924275X/

If you're struggling with specific issues, please see
http://adv-r.had.co.nz/Reproducibility.html
for how to post a fully working example of your issue so this group can understand what you have and what you want.

Lastly, good luck.

B

